entry.summary:
A running solution where you can add server middleware to ASP.NET Core minimal APIs Install the MCP packages from NuGet. Use the latest stable versions where possible. Example package links: ModelContextProtocol ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore Register the MCP server and transports during host building. WithToolsFromAssembly() scans your assembly for [McpServerToolType] classes and auto-registers tools. builder.Services .AddMcpServer() .WithHttpTransport() .WithToolsFromAssembly();
var app = builder.Build();
app.MapEndpoints(); // Your own extension method, defined later app.MapMcp(pattern: "api/mcp"); // Expose MCP over HTTP
await app.RunAsync();
Mark the types that contain tools with the appropriate attribute McpServerToolType and annotate tool methods McpServerTool. Prov…
